            <ArticleTitle>[Cavernous hemangioma of the masseter muscle. A contribution to the differential diagnosis of painful parotid tumors].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>88-90</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A sensitive tumor in the anterior parotid region of a young woman intraoperatively proved to be a cavernous hemangioma in the masseter muscle. The pronounced sensitivity of this small tumor suggested a malignant growth, especially an adenoid-cystic carcinoma, which frequently causes chronic pain already in an early stage.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
